----- stdout -----
Inspect or synchronize the current program's identity.

Run without a subcommand to compare the source `declare_id!` with the conventional local keypair. `pina keys sync` explicitly updates only that string literal after validating an unambiguous declaration and keypair.

Usage: pina keys [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  show
          Show the source and local keypair program IDs without changing files
  sync
          Update the source `declare_id!` from a validated local keypair
  new
          Generate a local keypair and synchronize the source program ID
  help
          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -p, --path <DIR>
          Inspect or synchronize a specific program crate. Defaults to the nearest project

      --keypair <KEYPAIR>
          Use KEYPAIR instead of `target/deploy/<program>-keypair.json`

      --json
          Emit a stable machine-readable JSON document

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  pina keys
  pina keys show --json
  pina keys --path ./programs/counter
  pina keys sync
  pina keys sync --keypair ./keys/counter-keypair.json
  pina keys new
  pina keys new --force

